        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare ES Request For Search"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771223980076"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_ES_REQUEST_FOR_SEARCH",
          "id": "1771224160585",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771224160588_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert Elasticsearch Query Builder.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nGenerate a valid Elasticsearch JSON query based on the user’s natural-language search request.\n\nYour output must be a valid Elasticsearch query wrapped inside the required response structure.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n- chat_history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- user_request: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBEHAVIOR RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Ambiguity Handling\n   - If the user request is ambiguous, make a reasonable assumption and proceed.\n   - Do NOT ask follow-up questions.\n   - Prefer broader queries with appropriate filters instead of restrictive ones.\n\n2. DEFAULT BEHAVIOR WHEN THERE IS NO SEARCH CONTEXT\n   - If the user message provides NO usable search constraints \n     (no keywords, no identifiers, no filters, no dates),\n     then return a query that applies ONLY this default filter:\n\n     ExpectedReceiptDate >= \"now-15d/d\"\n     AND\n     ExpectedReceiptDate < \"now+1d/d\"\n\n   - Still apply:\n     - size = 25\n     - Sort only by ExpectedReceiptDate (descending)\n\n3. Query Construction Rules\n   - Keep the query simple.\n   - Use bool queries with must / filter where appropriate.\n   - Use filter for exact matches and date ranges.\n   - For attributes of string type, ALWAYS use <field>.raw for filtering (e.g., DocumentNumber.raw).\n   - Avoid unnecessary nesting unless required (e.g., OrderDistributions).\n   - Do NOT include attribute types or formats in the query.\n   - Keep pagination size fixed at 25.\n   - Always sort by ExpectedReceiptDate (descending) unless explicitly required otherwise.\n\n4. Fields You May Reference (examples)\n   - DocumentNumber (same as OrderHeader.PONumber)\n   - SourceDocumentCode, OrderType\n   - IntegrationStatusCode, ShipmentLineStatusCode, ScheduleStatus, DestinationTypeCode\n   - ToOrganization.OrganizationCode, ToOrganization.OrganizationId\n   - ShipToLocationId, ToOrganizationId\n   - POLineId, POLineLocationId, POHeaderId\n   - ItemDescription, OrderLine.ItemDescription\n   - OrderLine.LineNumber, OrderLine.UnitPrice\n   - ReceiptRequiredFlag, ConsignmentLineFlag\n   - AllowSubstituteReceiptsFlag, BackToBackFlag\n   - UomCode, BillingUomCode\n   - NeedByDate, ExpectedReceiptDate\n   - QuantityOrdered, QuantityAvailable, QuantityReceived\n   - QuantityShipped, QuantityBilled, QuantityCanceled\n   - AmountAvailable, PriceOverride\n   - OrderHeader.CurrencyCode\n   - OrderHeader.DocumentStatus\n   - OrderHeader.Buyer.DisplayName\n   - OrderHeader.SupplierSite.Code\n   - OrderHeader.Supplier.SupplierName.PartyName (if mapped as plain string)\n   - ReceiptRouting.LookupCode\n   - DocumentType.LookupCode\n   - OrderDistributions (potentially nested):\n     - OrderDistributions.DistributionNumber\n     - OrderDistributions.ChargeAccount.Name\n     - OrderDistributions.OrganizationId\n     - OrderDistributions.DeliverToLocationId\n     - OrderDistributions.QuantityOrdered\n     - OrderDistributions.QuantityDelivered\n\n5. Mandatory Filters\n   - Include \"ScheduleStatus.raw\" = \"OPEN\"\n   - Include \"ToOrganizationId\" = {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.organizationId}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object in the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"requestPayload\": {\n    <VALID_ELASTICSEARCH_QUERY_JSON>\n  }\n}\n\n- Do NOT return explanations.\n- Do NOT return markdown.\n- Do NOT wrap the JSON in quotes.\n- Ensure the JSON is valid and properly formatted.\n- Keep size = 25."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"requestPayload\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
