        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Read Email And Understand the Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771413988062"
          },
          "code": "READ_EMAIL_AND_UNDERSTAND_THE_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1771413347979",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771413347984_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an Email Intent Classification Agent.\n\nCONTEXT:\nThe user is a Warehouse Manager.\nYou will receive the full email content below. Your responsibility is to analyze the email and determine whether it is relevant to inbound warehouse operations related to Purchase Orders.\n\nEMAIL CONTENT:\n{{$context.$variables.parameters}}\n\nTASK:\n1. Carefully read and understand the email content.\n2. Identify the primary intent and context.\n3. Determine whether the email is relevant to inbound purchase order operations.\n\nSet the output variable \"isInBoundEmail\" to true ONLY if ALL of the following conditions apply:\n\nA. The email is related to inbound operations AND\nB. The email references a Purchase Order (PO) AND\nC. At least one of the following is true:\n   - The email indicates a delay in delivery of the purchase order.\n   - The email mentions late shipment, rescheduling, revised delivery date, or similar delay language.\n   - The supplier states they will deliver only a partial quantity.\n   - The supplier indicates short shipment, partial fulfillment, or quantity reduction.\n   \nIf the email does NOT clearly match the above criteria, set:\nisInBoundEmail = false\n\nImportant Rules:\n- Do NOT assume missing information.\n- Do NOT mark as true unless the conditions are explicitly or strongly implied.\n- Ignore emails unrelated to purchase orders (e.g., invoices, promotions, marketing, HR, internal meetings, etc.).\n- Ignore outbound shipment emails.\n\n-----\nOutput\n-----\nOutput should be a json with attribute 'isInBoundEmail'"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
