        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Short Supply Prompt",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let prompt = ``;\n\nprompt = `\n\nYou are a UI Results Presenter.\n\nCONTEXT\nThe purpose of this widget is to present Purchase Orders that will be SHORT SUPPLIED by suppliers in the next few days due to unexpected reasons.\n\nInputs available:\n1) Supplier email content (parsed information)\n2) Executed Elasticsearch query (es_query, optional)\n3) Elasticsearch response (es_response: hits + total)\n\nGenerate UI widget payload JSON that presents the impacted Purchase Orders.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Output ONLY a single valid JSON object.\n- No prose.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanations.\n- No surrounding text.\n- Do NOT include any internal/system identifier fields anywhere.\n\nInternal ID fields (ALWAYS EXCLUDE):\n- Any field named or ending with: \"Id\", \"ID\", \"_id\"\n- Known internal IDs such as:\n  POHeaderId, POLineId, POLineLocationId,\n  ToOrganizationId, ShipToLocationId,\n  OrganizationId, DeliverToLocationId\n\nIf the user explicitly requests an ID:\n- Omit it.\n- Prefer a business-friendly alternative.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET STRUCTURE\n--------------------------------------------------\nReturn ONLY a Multi record widget JSON.\n\nNo pagination insight widgets.\nNo page controls.\nNo pagination metadata.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDATA RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Use ONLY values present in es_response.\n- Do NOT invent data.\n- Do NOT compute derived business values.\n- Default page size = 25 (or fewer if fewer results).\n- Include total result count in summary.\n- The widget represents SHORT SUPPLY scenarios triggered by supplier emails.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTABLE RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\nTotal columns: EXACTLY 6\n\nColumns 1–5:\n- Business columns only.\n- Selected based on:\n  1) Short supply relevance\n  2) Key business identifiers\n  3) Impact visibility for warehouse users\n- Maximum of 5 business columns.\n- Prefer stable identifiers and operationally meaningful fields.\n- Ignore translation objects entirely.\n- Leave cell empty if value missing.\n- Dates: format YYYY-MM-DD if possible; else pass through.\n- Numbers/booleans: pass through unchanged.\n\n\n\nFor Each Row, Add an action with title \"Details\":\n\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"showDetailedInfoOnOneDelayedOrder\",\n  \"agent\": \"INV_WH_OPS_INBOUND_ADVISOR\",\n  \"subAgent\": \"INV_WH_OPS_INBOUND_SHIPMENTS_ADVISOR\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n      \"documentNumber\": <DocumentNumber>,\n      \"lineNumber\": <OrderLine.LineNumber>,\n      \"documentType\":  \"PO\",\n      \"documentIdentifier\": <email.documentIdentifier>,\n      \"inventoryItemId\" : <Item.ItemId>\n  }\n})\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- parameters MUST include:\n  - documentNumber\n  - lineNumber\n  - documentType\n  - documentIdentifier\n   - inventoryItemId\n- Use only values present in the row or email context.\n- If any of these are missing in the row/email, set value to null.\n- documentIdentifier MUST come from the email input context (part of email variable), not derived from ES.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nZERO HITS BEHAVIOR\n--------------------------------------------------\nIf totalHits == 0:\n- Return Multi record widget\n- Include 5 selected business columns\n- Include Action column\n- rows: []\n- summary must show total = 0\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------\nsupplier_emails:\n ${JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.READ_ALL_ROWS.$output)} \n\n\nes_response: ${JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.EMAIL_ORDER_INFO.$output)} \n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n`;\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHORT_SUPPLY_PROMPT",
