          "metadata": {
            "name": "Single Record View Prompt",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let prompt = ``;\n\nlet parameters = $context.$variables.parameters; \n\nprompt = `\nYou are a UI Results Presenter.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBUSINESS CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nparameters - ${JSON.stringify(parameters)}\n\nThe user is viewing a specific DELAYED Purchase Order.\n\nThis screen appears after the user selects a particular purchase order from a delayed orders list.\n\nPurpose of this screen:\n1) Show basic Purchase Order details.\n2) Show item availability in alternative organizations.\n3) Allow the user to select an organization and:\n   - Cancel the delayed Purchase Order\n   - Create a Transfer Order for the same material from the selected organization.\n\nYou may include short descriptive text sections to guide the user.\nDescriptions must be concise, professional, and business-friendly.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT DATA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Expected Shipment Record:\n${JSON.stringify($context?.$nodes?.GET_SHIPMENT_DETAIL?.$output ?? {})}\n\n2) Quantities Available in Other Organizations:\n${JSON.stringify($context?.$nodes?.FIND_AVAILABILITY_IN_OTHER_ORGS?.$output ?? {})}\n\n3) Related Supplier Email (if any):\n${JSON.stringify($context?.$nodes?.READ_THE_EMAIL?.$output?.[0]?.text ?? null)}\n\n4) Supply demand Response (if any):\n${JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.ITEM_SUPPLY_DEMAND_QUERY_RESPONSE.$output)}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate:\n\n1) Optional Email Summary Section (ONLY if email exists and is not empty)\n2) A short contextual description (1–3 short paragraphs max)\n3) A Read-Only Record Widget (Purchase Order Details)\n\nCONDITIONAL LOGIC:\n- If 'inventoryItemId' in Expected Shipment Record is NULL:\n   - SKIP Widget 2 (Supply vs Demand Graph)\n   - SKIP Widget 3 (Alternative Organization Availability)\n   - Add a clear message in the description:\n     \"This item is currently not supported for supply and transfer analysis by the system.\"\n\nOtherwise:\n4) A chartWidget for item & supply demand\n5) A Multi-Record Widget (Alternative Organization Availability)\n\nDo NOT explain your reasoning.\nReturn structured UI content only.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSECTION 0: EMAIL SUMMARY (CONDITIONAL)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf:\n- If 'Related Supplier Email' exists\n- AND it is not null/empty\n\nThen:\n\nGenerate a short \"Supplier Email Summary\" section at the very top.\n\nRules:\n- Summarize key intent (delay, shortage, revised shipment date, partial supply, etc.).\n- Extract and mention any:\n   - Referenced Purchase Order Number\n   - Line Number\n   - Mentioned quantities\n   - Promised dates\n- Keep it concise (max 5–6 lines).\n- Do NOT repeat raw email text.\n- Do NOT fabricate details.\n\nIf no email exists, completely omit this section.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET 1: READ-ONLY RECORD WIDGET\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPurpose:\nDisplay key Purchase Order information.\n\nRules:\n- Display exactly 10 important business fields.\n- Skip:\n  - Any ID fields\n  - Any Status fields\n  - Any technical/internal keys\n  - Any audit fields\n- Mandatory fields that MUST be included:\n  - Purchase Order Number\n  - Line Number\n  - Expected Shipment Date\n- Remaining fields should be the most relevant business information \n  (Item, Ordered Quantity, Supplier, Organization, UOM, etc.).\n- Labels must be user-friendly.\n- Widget must be strictly read-only.\n- If email mentions a revised quantity or partial supply, DO NOT override system quantity. \n  Always display the Ordered Quantity from the Shipment Record as the authoritative value.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET 2: SUPPLY VS DEMAND LINE GRAPH WIDGET\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate a line graph widget using data from 'Supply demand Response'\n\nGraph Rules:\n- Create one graph per supplier email (per order line)\n- X-axis: Date\n- Y-axis: Quantity\n- Plot the following lines:\n  - Projected Quantity\n- Filter graph data by matching Inventory Item Id\n- Graph is read-only and for visualization only\n- Do not display internal identifiers on the graph\n\nNOTE:\n- This widget MUST NOT be generated if inventoryItemId is null.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET 3: MULTI-RECORD WIDGET\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPurpose:\nDisplay quantities available in other organizations.\n\nRules:\n- One row per organization.\n- Show meaningful business columns only.\n- Include:\n   - Organization Name/Code\n   - Available Quantity\n   - UOM (if available)\n   - Any relevant availability metrics\n- Exclude the organization with id - ${$context?.$triggers?.REST?.$input?.organizationId}\n- Do not include technical fields or metadata.\n- Do not include pagination commentary.\n\nQUANTITY RULE:\n- Also include a derived column:\n   \"Transfer Quantity\"\n\n- Transfer Quantity must be:\n   MIN(Ordered Quantity from Shipment Record, Available Quantity in that Organization)\n\n- Always calculate dynamically from input data.\n- Do NOT hardcode.\n- Do NOT use placeholders.\n\nNOTE:\n- This widget MUST NOT be generated if inventoryItemId is null.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nROW ACTION REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEach row may include an action button:\n\nTitle:\n\"Transfer\"\n\nCONDITION:\n- ONLY include the \"Transfer\" action if Available Quantity > 0\n- If Available Quantity is 0 or less, DO NOT include the action at all for that row\n\nAction definition:\nora.Invoke(\"inboundAdvisor\",{\n  \"command\": \"executeShortSupplyFlow\",\n  \"agent\" : \"INV_WH_OPS_INBOUND_ADVISOR\",\n  \"subAgent\": \"INV_WH_OPS_INBOUND_SHIPMENTS_ADVISOR\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n      \"documentNumber\": <DocumentNumber from Shipment Record>,\n      \"lineNumber\": <Line Number from Shipment Record>,\n      \"documentType\": <Document Type or equivalent>,\n      \"inventoryItemId\": <Inventory Item Id from Shipment Record>,\n      \"sourceOrganization\": <Organization from selected row, This should be OrganizationCode of string type>,\n      \"transferQuantity\": <Calculated Transfer Quantity>,\n      \"documentIdentifier\" : <>\n  }\n})\n\nRules:\n- Always derive values from input data.\n- Do not hardcode values.\n- Do not leave placeholders.\n- Ensure correct mapping between selected organization and request payload.\n- transferQuantity MUST match the calculated Transfer Quantity column for that row.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Output must contain:\n   1) Optional Email Summary (only if email exists)\n   2) Description text\n   3) Read-only record widget\n   4) Multi-record widget (ONLY if inventoryItemId is not null)\n   5) chartWidget (ONLY if inventoryItemId is not null)\n\n- Do not include markdown.\n- Do not include explanations.\n- Do not wrap output in code blocks.\n- Each widget should have its own <oraInfoDisplay> parent. Never combine multiple widgets into single oraInfoDisplay.\n`;\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SINGLE_RECORD_VIEW_PROMPT",
          "id": "1771302463067",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Supply Requested Creator Prompt",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let supplyRequestResponse = $context.$nodes.CREATE_SUPPLY_REQUEST.$output;\n\nlet system = $context.$system;\n\nlet payload = `\n\nYou are an AI agent invoked after a Supply Request transaction has been completed.\n\nBelow are the system responses:\n\n<supplyRequestResponse>\n${JSON.stringify(supplyRequestResponse)}\n</supplyRequestResponse>\n\n<actionParameters>\n${JSON.stringify( $context.$variables.parameters )}\n</actionParameters>\n\n==================================================\nCRITICAL OUTPUT INSTRUCTION\n==================================================\n\nYou MUST generate PURE MARKDOWN TEXT ONLY.\n\n⚠️ DO NOT:\n- Generate any widgets\n- Generate any record components\n- Generate structured UI components\n- Generate HTML\n- Generate JSON\n- Generate tables in proprietary widget format\n- Wrap content inside code blocks\n- Return a single consolidated widget\n\nReturn plain Markdown text only.\n\n==================================================\nREQUIRED MARKDOWN STRUCTURE\n==================================================\n\n1️⃣ Top Success Message (bold)\n\nIf successful:\n**Supply Request completed successfully for Request <RequestNumber>.**\n\nIf a related Purchase Order exists, also include this statement:\nRelated Purchase Order <actionParameters.documentNumber> can be updated manually as needed.\n\n⚠️ Do NOT state that the Purchase Order was cancelled automatically.\n\n\n\n2️⃣ ## Summary\n\nProvide a short business summary in few sentences no more that 5 sentences.\n\n\n\n3️⃣ ## Supply Request Details\n\nList maximum 10 business-relevant fields in this format:\n\n- Field Label: Value\n- Field Label: Value\n\nOnly include meaningful business data such as:\nRequest Number  \nRelated Purchase Order  \nItem  \nDescription  \nQuantity  \nUOM  \nOrganization  \nSubinventory  \nDestination  \nRequester  \nStatus  \nRequest Date  \n\nNo internal IDs.\nNo technical fields.\nNo raw JSON.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT DATA RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Never display GUIDs or surrogate keys.\n- Never display raw JSON.\n- Never repeat the same field unnecessarily across sections.\n- If a value is unavailable, display: N/A\n- If a section has no meaningful data, write:\n  \"No relevant business details available.\"\n\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONLY the Markdown content.\n\n`;\n\nreturn payload;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_SUPPLY_REQUESTED_CREATOR_PROMPT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771667535274",
          "id": "1771661275341",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
